WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:08.332
Daisy rushed back to the shelter booth with Kaleem and Grace.

2
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:12.791
Tosca was louder than ever!

3
00:00:12.792 --> 00:00:17.207
And all the dogs were barking again.

4
00:00:17.208 --> 00:00:21.111
A man handed a leash back to a shelter volunteer.

5
00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:24.129
"I don't want a dog that barks a lot."

6
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.163
"But this dog rarely barks at all," the volunteer said.

7
00:00:28.164 --> 00:00:32.582
The man was already hurrying away, covering his ears.

8
00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:34.879
Other people were leaving too.

9
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.916
Daisy gulped. "This adoption event is turning into a disaster!"

10
00:00:40.917 --> 00:00:44.593
"It's because of that loud cat," Grace said.

11
00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:48.144
"Scamp! Please stop barking."

12
00:00:48.145 --> 00:00:52.153
"Cat! Cat! Cat!" Scamp barked.

13
00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:56.082
Joan bit her lip and turned to the shelter volunteers.

14
00:00:56.083 --> 00:00:59.416
"Try to get the dogs calmed down again.

15
00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:05.179
Meanwhile I'll find someone to drive Tosca back to the shelter."

16
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.957
"That's a really good idea!" Kaleem said.

17
00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:15.616
"No, it's not." Beatrice buzzed loudly in Daisy's ear.

18
00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:19.463
"That cat deserves a chance to be adopted too."

19
00:01:19.464 --> 00:01:22.305
Daisy was already thinking the same thing.

20
00:01:22.306 --> 00:01:26.166
But she couldn't talk to Tosca in front of Grace.

21
00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:31.913
"Um, Grace, why don't you go back and watch the band?" Daisy said.

22
00:01:31.914 --> 00:01:34.916
"Scamp will probably stop barking over there."

23
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:39.457
"Maybe." Grace looked unsure.

24
00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:44.525
But she led Scamp away.

25
00:01:44.526 --> 00:01:50.499
"Now I can try talking to Tosca again," Daisy whispered to Kaleem and Beatrice.

26
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.902
Luckily nobody else was at the cat tent.

27
00:01:53.903 --> 00:01:58.377
That was probably because so many dogs were barking nearby.

28
00:01:58.378 --> 00:02:04.619
"Tosca," Daisy said. "If you're not afraid of dogs, then why do you keep yowling?"

29
00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.400
The cat finally stopped yowling to answer.

30
00:02:08.401 --> 00:02:11.666
"I'm just expressing myself.

31
00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:15.962
My first owner, Antonio, loved when I did that."

32
00:02:15.963 --> 00:02:21.892
She twitched her tail. "My second owner, however . . ."

33
00:02:21.893 --> 00:02:25.332
"Who was your second owner?" Daisy asked.

34
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:32.837
"Her name was Margaret." Tosca growled.

35
00:02:32.838 --> 00:02:39.207
"When Antonio got a job overseas, Margaret begged to adopt me.

36
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:47.749
But then her neighbors complained for some reason, and she gave me to the shelter."

37
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.451
Beatrice buzzed closer.

38
00:02:50.452 --> 00:02:55.918
"You're good at helping animals, Daisy. Help Tosca find a home."

39
00:02:55.919 --> 00:02:59.404
Daisy felt worried. "I'd like to.

40
00:02:59.405 --> 00:03:02.666
But Joan is about to send her back to the shelter."

41
00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:07.837
Tosca looked sad. "I don't like the shelter.

42
00:03:07.838 --> 00:03:11.707
The people are nice, but they come and go.

43
00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:15.863
I like having a human to snuggle with.

44
00:03:15.864 --> 00:03:20.707
And it's too quiet except for the annoying dogs."

45
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:28.020
The cat's big eyes brightened. "Hey, maybe you could take me home."

46
00:03:28.021 --> 00:03:32.711
"I wish I could," Daisy said. "But my dad has asthma.

47
00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.041
I can't have any pets."

48
00:03:35.042 --> 00:03:40.416
Tosca's eyes turned to Kaleem. "What about him?"

49
00:03:40.417 --> 00:03:43.587
"Kaleem already has a cat," Daisy said.

50
00:03:43.588 --> 00:03:46.541
"I don't think his parents will let him get another one."

51
00:03:46.542 --> 00:03:50.197
But Tosca's request had given her an idea.

52
00:03:50.198 --> 00:03:53.337
"We'll talk to people here at the fair," Daisy said.

53
00:03:53.338 --> 00:03:57.530
"I'm sure someone would love to adopt a nice cat like you."

54
00:03:57.531 --> 00:04:05.041
Tosca purred. "I miss having a nice owner like Antonio."

55
00:04:05.042 --> 00:04:08.615
Kaleem couldn't understand what Tosca was saying.

56
00:04:08.616 --> 00:04:12.422
But he could hear Daisy and figure out what she was planning.

57
00:04:12.423 --> 00:04:16.124
"Daisy, you'd better hurry," he said.

58
00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:24.594
"It won't be easy to find an adopter before Joan comes back!"

